00:00:00.679 --> 00:00:04.910
Hello and welcome to this video in which we
will look at how you can carry out a Kaizen

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:07.890
activity and establish measurable improvements.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:13.299
Carrying out a Kaizen activity involves
a systematic approach to identify,

00:00:13.819 --> 00:00:17.769
implement, and measure improvements
in various aspects of an organisation.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:23.700
For example, you may wish to establish measurable
improvements across areas such as costs,

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:29.130
health and safety, quality improvement, and
customer satisfaction, as well as many others.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:30.910
So how do we do this?

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:38.260
The first step is to clearly define the objective
of the Kaizen activity, focusing on a specific

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.830
area or process that requires improvement.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:47.310
At this step, you will set specific and
measurable goals for each improvement area.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.950
In this video, we will look at
how to reduce the setup time for a

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.120
manufacturing process as an example.

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:56.150
Assemble a cross functional team.

00:00:56.150 --> 00:01:01.200
Create a team comprising individuals
from different departments or areas who

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.169
have expertise or are directly involved
in the targeted improvement area.

00:01:05.729 --> 00:01:10.470
This cross functional team brings diverse
perspectives and ensures representation

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.150
from all relevant stakeholders.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:14.845
Analyse the current state.

00:01:15.605 --> 00:01:20.105
Conduct a thorough analysis of the current
state of the process targeted for improvement.

00:01:20.985 --> 00:01:26.445
Map out the current setup process, identify
steps that contribute to setup time, and

00:01:26.445 --> 00:01:28.655
document the time taken for each step.

00:01:29.205 --> 00:01:34.925
Use tools like value stream mapping or process
flowcharts to visualize the process utilisation.

00:01:36.185 --> 00:01:37.765
Generate improvement ideas.

00:01:38.535 --> 00:01:43.684
Conduct a brainstorming session with a team
to generate ideas for reducing setup time.

00:01:44.285 --> 00:01:49.294
Some ideas could include improving tool
organization, standardising setup procedures,

00:01:49.625 --> 00:01:51.514
or implementing quick change tooling.

00:01:52.774 --> 00:01:54.865
Prioritise improvement opportunities.

00:01:55.644 --> 00:02:00.215
Evaluate the generated ideas based on
their potential impact and feasibility.

00:02:00.775 --> 00:02:06.035
Prioritise the ideas that are likely to have the
most significant impact on reducing setup time.

00:02:07.285 --> 00:02:09.095
Establish measurable metrics.

00:02:09.685 --> 00:02:15.035
Define a metric to measure setup time, such as
the total time taken from stopping production

00:02:15.285 --> 00:02:17.335
to restarting production after setup.

00:02:17.935 --> 00:02:22.405
Set a specific target for reducing
setup time, for example, by 50%.

00:02:23.895 --> 00:02:25.075
Develop an action plan.

00:02:25.654 --> 00:02:31.165
Create a detailed action plan outlining the
steps, responsibilities, and timelines for

00:02:31.175 --> 00:02:33.394
implementing the selected improvement ideas.

00:02:33.994 --> 00:02:38.345
Assign team members to each task,
such as designing and implementing a

00:02:38.345 --> 00:02:42.925
tool organisation system, or creating
standardised setup instructions.

00:02:44.195 --> 00:02:45.555
Implement the improvements.

00:02:46.114 --> 00:02:49.524
Execute the action plan by implementing
the identified improvements.

00:02:50.105 --> 00:02:55.295
For example, create labeled and organised
tool storage areas, train operators on

00:02:55.295 --> 00:02:59.714
the standardised setup procedures, and
implement quick change tooling systems.

00:03:00.985 --> 00:03:02.375
Measure and track results.

00:03:02.954 --> 00:03:06.524
Measure the setup time before and
after implementing the improvements.

00:03:07.114 --> 00:03:12.355
Collect data on the time taken for each
step and calculate the overall setup time.

00:03:12.915 --> 00:03:16.545
Compare the results to the target
set in step five to assess the

00:03:16.545 --> 00:03:18.554
effectiveness of the Kaizen activity.

00:03:19.795 --> 00:03:21.834
Review, adjust, and sustain.

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:25.430
Review the results and gather
feedback from the team.

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:29.990
Identify any further opportunities
for improvement and make adjustments

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:32.010
to the setup process as necessary.

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:37.409
Develop standard operating procedures and
provide training to sustain the improvements.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:39.939
Celebrate achievements.

00:03:40.529 --> 00:03:45.180
Celebrate the successful reduction in setup
time and acknowledge the efforts of the team.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:50.810
Share the results and lessons learned with
the wider organisation to inspire others and

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:53.160
promote a culture of continuous improvement.

